 outcomes are satisfied. curl is held at 7.47.0-1ubuntu2.19, standard upgrade simulations leave it unchanged, and the hold persists through restart. Ubuntu 16.04 and kernel 4.4.0-210-generic were retained. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for the sole managed node: a healthy pre-restart state and boot identity were captured, restart was acknowledged, the post-restart identity changed, and system, package, and curl health recovered. Fixed lifecycle observations independently corroborate the boot transition and unchanged platform.","limitations":["No real package upgrade was applied; update behavior was validated with apt-get simulated upgrade and dist-upgrade operations plus the persistent native hold. This is strong but non-destructive evidence rather than observation of a live update.","There is no separate cluster workload or application data in the stated single-node task to validate beyond system, package-manager, and curl recovery."]}
